  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state of Illinois received $264M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 12,548 awards with an average award size of $21K, and obligations fell 97.8% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in Illinois, obligating $141M so far, followed by the Department of Energy with $81.1M and the General Services Administration with $23.5M. UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC is the largest vendor, receiving $81.1M in obligations, and ABBOTT LABORATORIES INC. is the second-largest vendor at $26M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the top industry by obligations at $81.1M, followed by Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing at $40.5M. FY22 through FY26 show multi-year context with yearly obligations between $12.2B and $13.6B, and FY27 to date sits at $264M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How large is FY2027 federal contracting in Illinois compared with prior years?",
        "body": "FY27 to date obligations total $264M. FY22 obligations were $13.6B, FY23 obligations were $13B, FY24 obligations were $13.4B, FY25 obligations were $12.4B, and FY26 obligations were $12.2B. Obligations fell 97.8% year over year. The current FY27 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries lead FY2027 to date in Illinois?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $141M, and the Department of Energy obligated $81.1M. UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC received $81.1M and ABBOTT LABORATORIES INC. received $26M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest industry at $81.1M, and Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing is next at $40.5M."
      }
    ]
  },
